These headers are the fixture of the `library_fixture` self-test hook of `cerastes verify` (decision 0046 item 10):
the driver compiles this directory in as a second library directory, ahead of the platform's include path, so
`#include <lib_*.h>` finds them, and they are verified like user code, not skipped like system headers.  They
exist to test what vlibc does not hold yet (predicates, pure functions, bodies, an untagged contract).  The tests
are `LibraryFixtureTests` in scripts/test_run_tests.py; they are not under tests/, so the harness's helper-header
rules do not apply.  Do not add a header here that a test does not use.
